# .NET build output
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.swp

# Publish output. Root-anchored, and that matters: an unanchored `dist/` also matched
# src/PackProphet.App/wwwroot/lib/bootstrap/dist/, which silently kept every vendored
# Bootstrap file out of the repo. Locally the app looked fine; on GitHub Pages the whole
# stylesheet 404'd and the app rendered with no Bootstrap variables or utilities at all.
/publish/
/dist/

# Tooling
.vs/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/

# Python bytecode, from the diagnostic tool under tools/DiagProbe. Anchored nowhere in
# particular because it appears next to whichever script was run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local sync credentials. Blazor layers appsettings.Development.json over appsettings.json, so this
# is how `dotnet run` reaches a real Supabase project while the committed file stays the placeholder
# a fork builds against. The deployed values come from repository variables — see deploy-pages.yml.
src/PackProphet.App/wwwroot/appsettings.Development.json

# Card art for sets the art CDN has not published yet. The deploy workflow writes this into the
# PUBLISHED output and never into the tree -- see tools/vendor-gap-art.py and the note in
# ArtSource -- but the script takes an --out, and pointing it here to try it out must not turn six
# megabytes of card art into a commit that stays in the history forever.
src/PackProphet.App/wwwroot/art/
